  "evidences": [
    {
      "id": "ev_1",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_DarkUniverse-APT-framework27(11-05-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s1"
      },
      "text": "securelist.com /darkuniverse-the-mysterious-apt-framework-27/94897 In April 2017, ShadowBrokers published their well-known ‘Lost in Translation’ leak, which, among other things, contained an interesting script that checked for traces of other APTs in the compromised system.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_2",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_DarkUniverse-APT-framework27(11-05-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s2"
      },
      "text": "In 2018, we found an APT described as the 27 function of this script, which we call ‘DarkUniverse’.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_3",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_DarkUniverse-APT-framework27(11-05-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s3"
      },
      "text": "ItaDuke is an actor known since 2013.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_8",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_DarkUniverse-APT-framework27(11-05-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s8"
      },
      "text": "The executable file embedded in the documents extracts two malicious files from itself, updater.mod and glue30.dll, and saves them in the working directory of the malware – %USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Roaming\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Reorder.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_9",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_DarkUniverse-APT-framework27(11-05-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s9"
      },
      "text": "After that, it copies the legitimate rundll32.exe executable into the same directory and uses it to run the updater.mod library.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_34",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_DarkUniverse-APT-framework27(11-05-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s12"
      },
      "text": "The updater.mod module uses the Win API function SetWindowsHookExW to install hooks for the keyboard and to inject glue30.dll into processes that get keyboard input.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_35",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_DarkUniverse-APT-framework27(11-05-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s13"
      },
      "text": "After that, glue30.dll loads and begins intercepting input in the context of each hooked process.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_36",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_DarkUniverse-APT-framework27(11-05-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s14"
      },
      "text": "The msvcrt58.sqt module intercepts unencrypted POP3 traffic to collect email conversations and victims’ credentials.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
